CaFS (384).png|Enhanced Reflexes
CaFS (360).png|Electricity Resistance
EoMF (277).png|Wall Scaling
TUE1 (162).png|Strong Horn
</gallery>{{Quote|"You couldn't eat the ground to charge up?"<br>"It's good, but this stuff is '''delicious'''."|[[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] reacting to Eatle eating [[Kevin's Car (Original)|his car]]'s bumper.<ref name="OM"/>}}
Similar to [[Upchuck]], Eatle has the ability to eat just about anything{{Refn|[[:File:Eatle Can Eat Just About Anything.PNG]]|group = DJW}} and then convert the materials' matter into energy to shoot a green laser beam out of the slot on his horn. The beam is powerful enough to cut a floating mountain of [[Legerdomain]] in half<ref name="EoMF">''[[Enemy of My Frenemy]]''</ref> and even hold down a [[Lucubra]]-enhanced [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]].<ref name="TUEP1" />

Eatle's jaws are very strong and can be used to chew up various resilient materials, like metal.<ref name="OM">''[[OTTO Motives]]''</ref>

Eatle has enhanced strength, as he was able to crush [[Captain Nemesis]]'s glove,<ref name="CaFS" /> grab a [[Ship]]-enhanced [[Julie Yamamoto|Julie]] before pushing her through several walls of her house without stopping,<ref>''[[Night of the Living Nightmare]]''</ref> and rip off the bumper of [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]]'s [[Kevin's Car (Original)|car]].<ref name="OM" />

Eatle has enhanced durability, as seen when he was able to withstand Captain Nemesis's glove's laser, which was able to injure a [[Chronosapien]] and kill a [[Human (Classic)|human]] with a single shot,<ref name="CaFS">''[[Catch a Falling Star]]''</ref> as well as an entire building from [[Dagon]]'s [[Dagon's Dimension|dimension]] falling on top of him.<ref name="TUEP1" />

Eatle can run very fast, and in addition to shooting lasers, his horn can also be used as a very effective battering ram; both of these feats were shown during his fight with Vilgax.<ref name="TUEP1" />

Eatle can scale up walls, as shown when he clambered up the [[Sorcerer's Engine]].<ref name="EoMF" />

==Weaknesses==
[[File:LDtTWA (39).png|thumb|Uncontrollable Hunger]]
Eatle may unaccountably try to eat something against his interests, such as the remains of the [[Tenn-Speed]].<ref>''[[Let's Do the Time War Again]]''</ref>

Being an [[Oryctini]], Eatle is weak against his natural predator.{{Refn|[[:File:Eatle Predator.png]]|group = DJW|name = predator}}

==History==
===Ultimate Alien===
*Eatle first appeared in ''[[A Knight to Remember]]'', where he tried to stop [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]] from breaking the [[Seal]] but was instantly defeated by him.
*In ''[[Enemy of My Frenemy]]'', Eatle defeated a water creature that [[Addwaitya]] had created. Later, Eatle tried to devour [[Charmcaster (Classic)|Charmcaster]]'s machine before switching into [[Chromastone (Classic)|Chromastone]] once he realized he could not eat the entire machine.
* In ''[[Catch a Falling Star]]'', Eatle fought [[Captain Nemesis]], but was defeated by a mentally unstable [[Jennifer Nocturne]].
*In ''[[Night of the Living Nightmare]]'', Eatle defeated a [[Ship]]-enhanced [[Julie Yamamoto|Julie]] in a dream.
*In ''[[The Ultimate Enemy: Part 1]]'', Eatle battled [[Ultimate Vilgax]] with the help of [[Sir George]] before eventually switching into [[Humungousaur (Classic)|Humungousaur]] when Vilgax started gaining the upper hand.

===Omniverse===
*In ''[[Hot Stretch]]'', Eatle chased after [[Ester]] in [[Undertown]] and retrieved a [[Nuclear Fusion Device]] from her only to lose it to the [[Kraaho]].
*In ''[[Store 23]]'', Eatle briefly flew through the air due to being launched by [[Liam]]'s cart of [[Vaxasaurian (Classic)|Vaxasaurian]] eggs before reverting.
*In ''[[Return to Forever]]'', Eatle tried to break out of a force field, but was reverted by the [[Forever Knights]]' [[DNA Scanner]].
*In ''[[OTTO Motives]]'', Eatle briefly fought a giant [[OTTO]].
*In ''[[Let's Do the Time War Again]]'', Eatle ate part of the wrecked [[Tenn-Speed]] offscreen before being picked up by [[Rook Blonko|Rook]].
* In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Eatle appeared for a short time when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was cycling through his aliens.

